after the huge success of the first  season of daredevil on Netflix Marvel  continues to expand its universe on the  small screen with Jessica Jones based on  the character created by comic book  writer Brian Michael Bendis and artist  Michael Gaydos like its predecessor  Jessica Jones features 13 episodes for  about 50 minutes each the first episode  dives straight into the current day  story of superhero turned private  investigator Jessica Jones subsequent  episodes maintain an air of mystery as  they steadily reveal aspects of her  character building Jessica's world in  the present day while gradually  uncovering her tortured past via  traumatic visions and just as Marvel  approached daredevil as a crime drama  first in a superhero show second jessica  jones puts the focus on film noir and  psychological drama so expect many of  the usual moi trappings including a  cynical private detective voice-over  narration hard-boiled repartee  flashbacks and shadows cast by venetian  blinds if you enjoyed the grounded  grittiness and relative realism of  daredevil there's a lot for you to look  forward to in this new series which  again is set in Hell's Kitchen New York  and if you're into Easter eggs there's  plenty to keep your eyes and ears open  for - and I'll have a video on just that  once the full series is released this  week on Netflix oh and the show also  cleverly gears up for Marvel's next big  screen outing in 2016 Captain America  Civil War Breaking Bad's Kristen Rissa  is flat-out phenomenal in the lead  bringing the whiskey guzzling  tough-talking sarcasm spouting Jessica  to vivid life Reese is equally good at  spitting out darkly comic comebacks and  snubbing social niceties as she isn't  unveiling Jessica's disturbing demons  and delivering powerful punches as Luke  Cage actor Mike Colter shares great  chemistry with Ritter expect some pretty  intense scenes that are about as far  away as you can get from the pg-13  hookup that never was between the Hulk  and Black Widow and after seeing Colter  as caged in this series I'm looking  forward to his own Luke Cage series next  year like Daredevils Wilson Fisk David  Tennant's mind-controlling psycho  kilgrave's slowly but surely emerges  from the shadows as one hell of a creepy  villain Rachel Taylor  puts in a nicely understated turn as  Jessica's estranged best friend Trish  Walker who's a radio show host and  former child star as NYPD cop will  Simpson actor will travel provides solid  support and I can't shake the feeling  that travel has something of Chris Evans  is Captain America about him and carry  on Marcy's probably still best known as  Trinity in the Matrix movies puts in a  great turn as a cold and calculating  lawyer jeryn hogarth action wise from  the first seven episodes that I've seen  Jessica Jones isn't as visceral or  striking as daredevil though when there  is action it is well-executed  and just as daredevil doesn't flinch and  showing the brutal side of Matt Murdock  story Jessica Jones certainly doesn't  shy away from mature themes including  psychological and physical abuse and  blame and shame yet despite this dark  and serious side to Jessica Jones there  is a lot of humor in the series much of  it and surprisingly thanks to the show's  lead so although this series didn't grab  me quite as immediately as daredevil did  Jessica Jones is a show that grew on me  the more I watched it and I'm certainly  looking forward to seeing the final six  episodes so to sum up Marvel's Jessica  Jones is a more intense series that  matches great writing from showrunner  Melissa Rosenberg with a superb cast led  by a pitch-perfect performance from  Kristen Rissa Jessica Jones gets 4 out  of 5 flicks so guys are you looking  forward to Jessica Jones and if you've  seen it what did you think were you a  fan of Marvel's daredevil and what would  you like to see in the season 2 of that  series let me know in the comments below  once i've watched the final six episodes  of jessica jones I'll be making a  spoiler rific easter egg video for the  whole season  and I'll add an annotation here as soon  as it's live and as always do please  like share and comment and hit that  subscribe button for more videos like  this thanks for watching and see you  next time you be guy a superhero lovers  you
 

